{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And your desire shall be to your husband</b> — for relations. And even so, you will not have the audacity to demand it verbally, but he shall rule over you — all is from him and not from you. This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Genesis 3:16). And it is not correct, for this is a praise in women, as they said (Eruvin 100b): and this is a fine trait in women. And Rabbi Abraham said (Ibn Ezra on Genesis 3:16): 'Your desire shall be to your husband' means your obedience, and the sense is that you shall heed all that he commands you, for you are in his domain to do his will. But I have not found the term תְּשׁוּקָה except in the sense of longing and desire. And the correct interpretation in my eyes is that He punished her in that she will yearn greatly for her husband, and will not be sensitive to the distress of pregnancy and childbirth, and he will hold her as a maidservant. And the way of a slave is not to long to acquire a master for himself; rather, he would willingly flee from him. And behold, this is measure for measure: for she gave also to her husband and he ate at her command, and her punishment is that she will no longer command him, but he will command her as he pleases."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:24:20.911031549Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}